          "end": 249.63,
          "en": "with multiple projects inside of one Angular managed folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 249.63,
          "end": 251.73,
          "en": "this is how I would recommend that you do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 251.73,
          "end": 255.84,
          "en": "Create the project with NG new, your name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 255.84,
          "end": 259.53,
          "en": "and then dash dash create dash application set to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 259.53,
          "end": 262.2,
          "en": "Enter after, add your different applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 262.2,
          "end": 263.943,
          "en": "with the NG generate command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 264.93,
          "end": 268.68,
          "en": "Now also, of course, you cannot just generate applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 268.68,
          "end": 272.07,
          "en": "so web applications, you can also generate libraries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 272.07,
          "end": 273.723,
          "en": "Let's take a close look at that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
